From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Vickberg <wickbergster@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 29 Mar 2026 18:25:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: make MAC_PWR_SEL configurable from DT

qca8k_setup_mac_pwr_sel() sets the RGMII I/O voltage bits in MAC_PWR_SEL
(0x00e4) from the machine compatible: "qcom,ipq8064" puts RGMII0 at 1.8V
and "qcom,ipq8065" puts RGMII1 at 1.8V. That does not match the boards:

- Many ipq8064 boards (TP-Link C2600, Netgear R7500 and D7800, Linksys
  EA8500 and others) need RGMII1 at 1.8V and RGMII0 at 1.5V. Their
  swconfig initvals wrote 0x0006a545, DSA writes 0x000aa545. The
  NEC WG2600HP3 (ipq8062) also lists "qcom,ipq8064" and gets the same
  wrong value.
- The Netgear R7500 and R7500v2 use the same SoC and need opposite
  settings.
- ipq8065 boards also list "qcom,ipq8064", so both checks match and both
  interfaces end up at 1.8V. Their swconfig initvals set RGMII0 only.

With 0x000aa545 the C2600 stops receiving on the CPU port after hours
or days of traffic. Test builds that write 0x0006a545 have run for
months without it. Those builds also stopped forcing flow control on
the CPU ports, a change that is not part of this patch.

The voltage depends on the board wiring. Replace the compatible checks
with two boolean properties on the switch node:

  qca,mac-pwr-sel-rgmii0-1p8v: RGMII0 (MAC0, bit 19) at 1.8V
  qca,mac-pwr-sel-rgmii1-1p8v: RGMII1 (MAC5/MAC6, bit 18) at 1.8V

A set bit selects 1.8V, a clear bit 1.5V (QCA8337 datasheet 80-Y0619-3
Rev. D, table 5-43). The bits only matter with the internal regulator.
Device trees without either property keep the old compatible-based
setting, so existing DTBs behave as before and switches on other SoCs
are still left alone.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/18979
Signed-off-by: Alexander Vickberg <wickbergster@gmail.com>
[luminoso: fall back to the compatible checks when neither property is
 set, rename the properties to 1p8v, move the binding to its own patch,
 rewrite the description]
Signed-off-by: Guilherme Cardoso <luminoso@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c |   18 +++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -1066,17 +1066,21 @@ qca8k_setup_mac_pwr_sel(struct qca8k_pri
 	u32 mask = 0;
 	int ret = 0;
 
-	/* SoC specific settings for ipq8064.
-	 * If more device require this consider adding
-	 * a dedicated binding.
-	 */
-	if (of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,ipq8064"))
+	if (device_property_read_bool(priv->dev, "qca,mac-pwr-sel-rgmii0-1p8v"))
 		mask |= QCA8K_MAC_PWR_RGMII0_1_8V;
 
-	/* SoC specific settings for ipq8065 */
-	if (of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,ipq8065"))
+	if (device_property_read_bool(priv->dev, "qca,mac-pwr-sel-rgmii1-1p8v"))
 		mask |= QCA8K_MAC_PWR_RGMII1_1_8V;
 
+	/* Device trees without the properties keep the old SoC default */
+	if (!mask) {
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,ipq8064"))
+			mask |= QCA8K_MAC_PWR_RGMII0_1_8V;
+
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,ipq8065"))
+			mask |= QCA8K_MAC_PWR_RGMII1_1_8V;
+	}
+
 	if (mask) {
 		ret = qca8k_rmw(priv, QCA8K_REG_MAC_PWR_SEL,
 				QCA8K_MAC_PWR_RGMII0_1_8V |
